    <mxCell id="note" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-top:4px;text-align:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;HOW TO READ THIS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;/&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Solid&lt;/b&gt; = built in this 2-week iteration (bands A–D). &lt;b&gt;Grey dashed&lt;/b&gt; = the system’s functional scope, not yet built (bands E–G). Descoped is a schedule fact, not an absence of requirement — it belongs on the diagram so the gap is visible rather than forgotten (D12).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:6px 0 0 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Clean architecture.&lt;/b&gt; Every ellipse is one &lt;b&gt;interactor&lt;/b&gt; in the application layer. Left-hand actors drive it (CLI, scheduler, a person); right-hand actors are driven through gateway ports. Nothing inside the boundary knows about HTTP, SQL, StAX or CSV.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:6px 0 0 4px;&quot;&gt;That is why band E costs far less than it looks: &lt;i&gt;Screen one name (sync REST)&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;&#171;include&#187;&lt;/b&gt;s &lt;i&gt;Screen a name&lt;/i&gt;, which is already built. The REST controller is a driving adapter over an existing interactor — not a rewrite. The same holds for batch and re-screening.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:6px 0 0 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Security by design.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;Record audit event&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;Validate config at startup&lt;/i&gt; are use cases, not middleware. They sit inside the interactor, so no adapter can route around them — which is what Internal Audit will test. &lt;i&gt;Verify source fixture&lt;/i&gt; is included by every load, not just at onboarding: a mis-mapped name column loads cleanly and screens cleanly, and the fixture is the only thing that catches it.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="175" width="1150" x="140" y="1350" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
